  <p class="note">Everything uses the work steps that exist (<code>look</code>, <code>hold</code>, <code>wait</code>, <code>turn</code>, <code>choose</code>, <code>carry</code>); nothing new in the systems (17) or the crew sim (14) except one-line, typeof-guarded reads listed on each page.</p>
</section>

<section id="order">
  <h2>Proposed build order (four rounds; the build master merges after each)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Round</th><th>E1</th><th>E2</th><th>E3</th></tr>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>24 core on C's behalf: tool wear functions, <code>WORK_BANDS[2]</code>, the side-job cap; the Bunk 1 texts</td><td>M13 leak hunting</td><td><b>the places turn:</b> every Step 4 place on every deck in one turn (so the others can rely on them)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>M11 tool upkeep, M12 logbook</td><td>M14 irrigation, M15 rewiring</td><td>M10 workshop + tinkering</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>rounds stages 2-3, hauling stages 2-3 (with <code>manifestRun</code>)</td><td>M8 stage 2 (team parts, after E1's <code>manifestRun</code>), favour cases</td><td>cabin touches, star logging</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>(spare: fixes from review)</td><td>fault-finder tickets and the pin</td><td>M17 lift roof (if it slips, it ships after on its own)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Merge order inside a round, as the plan says: 24 core → mechanics in ladder order → cases → places → the writer's lines. Regressions on Decks 1-6 stay pixel-identical except where a page adds a place or a decal.</p>
</section>

<section id="seats">
  <h2>Seats for a small team (overnight cap)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Seat</th><th>Branch (as the plan's)</th><th>Owns tonight</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>E1</b>, mechanic engineer 1</td><td><code>claude/mech-rounds</code>, 0.45.x</td><td>24a, 24d stages, 24m, 24n; the 24 core lines on C's behalf; 15's texts on P's behalf</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>E2</b>, mechanic engineer 2</td><td><code>claude/mech-incidents</code>, 0.51.x</td><td>24h stage 2, 24o, 24r (irrigation; 24p is C2's first promotion), 24q (moved from M3 to balance), 24l's favour cases and tickets on H's behalf</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>E3</b>, mechanic engineer 3</td><td><code>claude/mech-diagnose</code>, 0.53.x</td><td>the places turn (seat A's job tonight), 24j, 24t (new: cabin and stars), 24s and the lift's two functions in 11</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>B</b>, build master</td><td><code>claude/integration-test</code></td><td>merges each round, runs every check, hands the lead a candidate on its own preview link</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>R</b>, reviewer</td><td>—</td><td>reviews each branch against the checklist and these pages (one owner per function, words not numbers, determinism twice, phone budget)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>W</b>, writer</td><td><code>claude/writer-p5</code></td><td>workshop orders and thank-yous, logbook summaries, leak and rewiring lines, the six favour cases, Calder's ticket Mail, star and cabin lines, the lift roof's lines</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Hash keys: 1010-1026 (1000-1004 are H2's; 1005-1009 left as H2's spare; nothing in any branch uses 1005+, checked 2026-10-19). Every new field lives under <code>SHIP.works.side</code> and is read defensively, so old saves load. A new check, if useful: <code>mech_check</code> grows a Step 4 section; <code>puzzle_check</code> covers the favour cases and tickets.</p>
</section>

<section id="calls">
  <h2>Lead's calls, for the user's morning review</h2>
  <p>Where the plan was vague, the simplest thing that fits:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Tool upkeep's lesson:</b> Torres is off on Thursdays and Fridays, so whoever's on shift teaches it, the first time you use your bench.</li>
    <li><b>Irrigation:</b> the first harvest Saturday on or after Day 13.</li>
    <li><b>Rewiring</b> starts Day 17 (the weekend and the second test days come first).</li>
    <li><b>The lift roof</b> is Thursdays 15:30-16:30 (not mid-morning: team jobs and tea), and crew wait for the lift for the hour rather than climb the ladder.</li>
    <li><b>The stocktake</b> is Thursdays 13:30, first on Day 18.</li>
    <li><b>Favour cases and tickets</b> are built by E2 from H's handover (no H seat tonight); H reviews later.</li>
    <li><b>Cabin touches and star logging</b> had no seat: E3, in a new sub-block 24t.</li>
    <li><b>Tier 2 reputation</b> keeps C2's numbers; side jobs give at most +2 a day so they never rush a promotion.</li>
    <li><b>The workshop's machines</b> are plain places for now, not machines that wear.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="check">
  <h2>Check-in 4: "a weekend of side jobs"</h2>
  <p>Start on Day 12 (Friday, an Officer): an order on the shop board, your bench, the log at 16:30. Days 13-14 (the weekend): a favour case, Calder's ticket Mail, the harvest's nozzles (if it's a harvest Saturday), stars at night, tinkering, your cabin. Then Days 17-18 for the weekday ones: rewiring, the stocktake, the lift roof.</p>
</section>

